-for-multi-step-strategies","content":"Smart Validation for Multi-Step Strategies"},"1681":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"How smart validation works"},"1682":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Opting into strict validation"},"1683":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"See also"},"1684":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Without in-loop validation, you get JSON that may or may not match your schema. You then have to write error handling, decide whether to retry, and figure out how to feed errors back."},"1685":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Struktur does all of this for you."},"1686":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Send the extraction prompt to the LLM."},"1687":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Validate the response with Ajv against the schema."},"1688":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If valid: return it."},"1689":{"id":"/d