at` (e.g., `date`, `email`) only when you need it — it adds validation surface."},"1697":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#observing-retries-with-events","content":"Use the `onMessage` event to see when retries happen:"},"1698":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#smart-validation-for-multi-step-strategies","content":"When using parallel or sequential strategies, your data might be split across multiple chunks. For example, an invoice's price might appear on page 1, while the vendor name appears on page 5. If both fields are `required` in your schema, validating intermediate results would fail unnecessarily."},"1699":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"},"1700":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Type errors** (`string` vs `number`) → Retry immediately"},"1701":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Format errors** (invalid email) → Retry immediately"},"1702":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Required field errors** → Allowed during intermediate steps"},"1703":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**All constraints** → Enforced on final validation"},"1704":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-29","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"This means the model can extract partial data without pressure to hallucinate missing required fields. The final validation ensures all required fields are present before returning."},"1705":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-30","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Disable smart validation with the `strict` flag:"},"1706":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-31","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Use `strict: true` when:"},"1707":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-32","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You know each chunk contains complete data"},"1708":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-33","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You want early failure on missing fields"},"1709":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-34","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You're debugging extraction issues"},"1710":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-35","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Extraction Pipeline — where validation fits"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-36","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"Events & Obse